{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>He has set me up</b> — he says it refers to the pain. And some say: to Eliphaz." "<b>to be a byword</b> — to be a proverb and a taunt." "<b>and you have set me before</b> — like a place of תפת before people and their eyes. And some say: that the final tav is added and it is like תוף."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:52.950307506Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}